        "officialText": "PERSONAL HYGIENE IN THE SECURITY WORKING ENVIRONMENT:\nTo prevent the spreading of diseases and maintaining a healthy and physical work force.\n\nBASIC RULES THAT A SECURITY OFFICER MUST ADHERE TO:\n\u2022 Personal cleanliness \u2013 a security officer must be clean at a personal level.\n\u2022 Always wear clean clothes: Dirty clothes are smelly and unhealthy. By washing your clothes, you remove odors and smells.\n\u2022 Avoid smoking & avoid spitting in public: Spitting in public is one of the most despicable acts done by a human being.\n\u2022 Have enough sleep & rest enough to remain alert during duty.\n\u2022 Shave regularly: Keep facial hair neat and professional.\n\u2022 Regular bathing: The skin must be washed regularly because it provides the body with protection against pollution and impurities.\n\u2022 Hair and head care: Keeping hair clean and short avoids sores, pimples, and prevents blocking pores.\n\u2022 Hand washing: Washing hands before meals and handling food avoids spreading diseases.\n\u2022 Dental care: Cleaning teeth regularly prevents germs from accumulating.\n\u2022 Foot care: Feet must always be clean and a clean pair of socks must be worn daily to avoid inflammation and bad odor.\n\u2022 Fingernails: Nails should be short and clean; dirty nails carry germs that contaminate food.\n\u2022 Exercise regularly to maintain fitness.",
