        "summary": "Hazard recognition, accident causes, and understanding the five categories of symbolic safety signs.",
        "officialText": "WHAT IS AN ACCIDENT?\nAn accident is defined as an undesirable event caused by unsafe acts and unsafe conditions resulting in damage to property or injury to people.\nAccidents do not just happen! They are caused by people acting in an unsafe way or resulting from an unsafe condition which has not been attended to.\n\nCAUSES OF ACCIDENTS:\n\u2022 Lack of knowledge\n\u2022 Physical or mental defect\n\u2022 Improper attitude\n\u2022 Inadequate work standards\n\u2022 Unsafe conditions\n\nSAFETY SIGNS CONSIST OF 3 PARTS:\n\u2022 Shape\n\u2022 Color\n\u2022 Pictogram (Picture)\n\nCATEGORIES OF SYMBOLIC SAFETY SIGNS:\n1. GENERAL INFORMATION: Square shape, green background, white picture. Gives direction arrows, emergency exits, and First Aid signs.\n2. FIRE INFORMATION: Square shape, red background, white picture. Indicates location of firefighting equipment.\n3. WARNING SIGNS: Triangular shape, yellow background, black border and picture. Warns of danger (e.g. wet floor, high voltage).\n4. MANDATORY SIGNS: Circular shape, blue background, white picture. Prescribes compulsory protective clothing (e.g. hard hat, safety boots).\n5. PROHIBITORY SIGNS: Circular shape, white background, red border, red cross bar, black picture. Prohibits activities (e.g. No Smoking).\n\nDANGERS OF SMOKING IN NON-SMOKING AREAS:\nFire, explosion, loss of lives, damage to property, and loss of production time.",
