        "officialText": "ROLE AND OBJECTIVE OF SECURITY:\nThe primary role of security is to protect life, property, and proprietary information.\n1. Prevent terrorist and adversary actions.\n2. Protect premises against sabotage, theft, and malicious damage.\n3. Ensure classified and confidential information is guarded against espionage.\n4. Support and cooperate with the South African Police Service (SAPS) in crime prevention and investigation.\n5. Create awareness among staff and the public regarding safety measures.\n\nTHREE MAIN CATEGORIES OF SECURITY FUNCTIONS:\n1. Physical Security (access control, fences, locks, alarms).\n2. Personnel Security (screening, vetting, identification).\n3. Information Security (safeguarding confidential documents, IT systems, and registers).\n\nCONTRIBUTIONS EXPECTED FROM SECURITY OFFICERS:\n\u2022 Treat all people with fairness, dignity, and respect.\n\u2022 Emphasize prevention over cure: proactive patrols detect crime before it occurs.\n\u2022 Protect classified information like a newborn baby; loss of secrets can paralyze a company.\n\u2022 Strictly enforce access rules: no unauthorized person enters the premises.",
