        "officialText": "ACTIONS UPON DISCOVERING A SUSPICIOUS OBJECT / BOMB:\n\u2022 DO NOT PANIC and DO NOT CAUSE PANIC.\n\u2022 DO NOT TOUCH, MOVE, OR JAR THE OBJECT: Do not try to be a hero!\n\u2022 Mark the location with a visible, recognizable object without getting too close.\n\u2022 Notify the control room or SAPS immediately.\n\u2022 Evacuate the immediate area calmly.\n\u2022 Do NOT use two-way radios or mobile phones in the immediate vicinity of the suspected bomb (radio frequency can trigger electronic detonators).\n\u2022 Turn off open flames and ensure fire exits are open.\n\nIMMEDIATE ACTION DRILLS AFTER A BOMB EXPLOSION:\n1. Remain calm; do not run aimlessly.\n2. Alert control room / SAPS / Emergency medical services.\n3. Render first aid to the injured if safe to do so.\n4. Assist in orderly evacuation along safe routes (avoid shattered glass).\n5. Cordon off the area and keep bystanders away to preserve evidence.\n6. Watch out for secondary devices (terrorists often plant a second bomb to hit first responders).\n7. Activate site emergency shutdown procedures.",
