        "summary": "Patrol principles, routes, security risks encountered on patrol, and guard uniform inspection.",
        "officialText": "PURPOSE OF PATROLLING:\nTo detect and prevent crime, fire, safety hazards, and protect the client's assets through active physical presence.\n\nTYPES OF PATROLS:\n\u2022 Foot patrol: Ideal for close inspection of doors, windows, and tight alleyways.\n\u2022 Mobile / Vehicle patrol: Covers vast premises, perimeters, and allows rapid response.\n\u2022 Static guard post: Stationed at a fixed vantage point or entrance.\n\nPRINCIPLES & EMERGENCY PROCEDURES OF PATROLLING:\n\u2022 Remain calm at all times.\n\u2022 Vary patrol routes and timing (never follow a predictable routine that criminals can time).\n\u2022 Stay alert and keep to shadows at night.\n\u2022 Check all doors, windows, locks, and perimeter fencing.\n\u2022 Carry essential equipment: Flashlight (torch), whistle, baton, pocket book, pen, and communication radio.\n\u2022 In emergencies: Stay calm, notify control room immediately, activate alarms if needed, and alert emergency teams.\n\nSECURITY RISKS ENCOUNTERED ON PATROL:\nBurglary, theft, arson, armed robbery, sabotage, trespassing, and industrial accidents.\n\nPHYSICAL AIDS ASSISTING THE PATROL OFFICER:\nPerimeter fencing, security gates, adequate lighting, locksets, intrusion alarms, guard dogs, and CCTV cameras.",
