        "title": "Use of Fire Extinguisher",
        "summary": "Fire extinguisher types, color code bands, classes of fire, and safety precautions when tackling fires.",
        "officialText": "CLASSES OF FIRE:\n\u2022 Class A: Combustible solids (wood, paper, textiles, plastics). Extinguished by Water or DCP.\n\u2022 Class B: Flammable liquids (petrol, oil, thinners, alcohol, paraffin). Extinguished by Foam, CO2, DCP. (NEVER use water!).\n\u2022 Class C: Electrical fires (switchboards, transformers, appliances). Extinguished by CO2 or DCP. (NEVER use water!).\n\u2022 Class D: Combustible metals (magnesium, sodium, potassium). Extinguished by specialized dry powder.\n\u2022 Class E: Flammable gasses (butane, methane, propane, acetylene). Extinguished by shutting off the gas supply and DCP.\n\nEXTINGUISHER COLOR LABELS / BANDS:\n\u2022 Water (H2O): Red label. Used on Class A fires only.\n\u2022 Carbon Dioxide (CO2): Black label. Used on Class B and electrical fires. Safe on electronics.\n\u2022 Dry Chemical Powder (DCP): Blue label. Multi-purpose for Class A, B, C.\n\u2022 Foam: Cream label. Used on flammable liquids (Class B).\n\u2022 Vaporizing Liquid / BCF: Green label. Halon replacement.\n\nSAFETY PRECAUTIONS BEFORE USING AN EXTINGUISHER:\n\u2022 Always ensure a safe escape route is open behind you.\n\u2022 Never attempt to fight a fire that is spreading too fast or too large.\n\u2022 Verify you have the correct extinguisher for that specific class of fire.\n\u2022 Check pressure gauge, pin, and nozzle for defects or sabotage.\n\u2022 Adopt a crouching posture when approaching flames and apply the extinguishing agent to the BASE of the fire using a sweeping motion.",
        "plainEnglish": "WHAT THIS MEANS IN EASY WORDS:\nFire needs three things to burn: Heat, Fuel, and Oxygen (The Fire Triangle).\n\u2022 If an electric heater or computer catches fire: NEVER throw water on it! You will get electrocuted and die! Use a black CO2 extinguisher or blue DCP extinguisher.\n\u2022 If petrol catches fire: Do NOT use water! The water will spread the burning petrol across the floor. Use foam or powder.\n\u2022 When shooting an extinguisher: Aim at the bottom/base of the flames, not the smoke on top!\n\u2022 Keep your back to the door so you can run away if the flames grow too big.",
