        "officialText": "THE FIVE C'S OF PROFESSIONAL SECURITY REPORTING:\n1. CLEAR: Plain, understandable language; no confusing jargon or ambiguous sentences.\n2. CONCISE: Brief and to the point; omit irrelevant gossip or opinions.\n3. COMPLETE: Contains all relevant facts answering Who, What, When, Where, Why, and How.\n4. CORRECT: 100% factual, accurate dates, times, names, and measurements.\n5. COURTEOUS: Professional, respectful, and objective tone.\n\nETHICS OF REPORT WRITING:\n\u2022 Honesty is the foundation: it is a severe criminal and disciplinary offence to falsify, forge, or exaggerate security reports.\n\u2022 Objective: The reporter must remain impartial, recording only what they saw, heard, or discovered without personal bias.\n\u2022 Format: Chronological sequence (step-by-step in order of time) with signed statements from witnesses.",
